gbdk-sys is in two parts, under different terms.

The Rust source in `src/` and the startup in `gbdk_init.s` are the author's own
work, under any one of:

    Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT

    licenses/LICENSE-ZLIB
    licenses/LICENSE-APACHE
    licenses/LICENSE-MIT

The archives in `lib/` (libgb.a, libsm83.a, crt0.o) are prebuilt from GBDK-2020
and SDCC and are redistributed here unmodified. The GBDK-2020 library is under
GPLv2 with a linking exception, and the zx0 decompression it contains is under
BSD 3-Clause:

    licenses/LICENSE_GPLV2_LE   GBDK-2020 library and makefiles
    licenses/LICENSE_SDCC       SDCC, from which parts of the library come
    licenses/LICENSE_ZX0        zx0 decompression in the library

GBDK-2020 states that a compiled ROM built with it carries no requirement to
include or credit these licenses, which is what the linking exception is for.
Redistributing the library itself, as this crate does, is a separate matter and
does carry them.

Sources: https://github.com/gbdk-2020/gbdk-2020
